/-!
# Kernel-checked finite part: packed literals (generated)

Generated by `scratch/gen_literals.py` of lane K (campaign `ProofRuns/2026-09-28_analytic_large_n`).
Nothing here is trusted: every lane of every literal is recomputed by kernel evaluation in
`Erdos993Lean/ZhangKernel/LiteralChecks.lean` (`bRow_ok`, `tabRow_ok`).

* `bRow m`: lane `r` (bits `64 r` to `64 r + 63`) is `C(m, r)` for `m, r < 64`.
* `tabRow h r`: lane `M` (64-bit lanes) is `2^62 + T_h(r, M)`, where `T_h(r, M)` is the largest
  value over `0 ≤ m ≤ M` of `x_h(r, m)`: `x_0(r, m) = C(m, r) − B(m, r)` (the path row `path(k)`
  against the matching bound), `x_1(r, m) = −B(m, r)` (the lower layer rule), `x_2(r, m) = B(m, r)`
  (the upper layer rule), with `B(m, r) = C(m, r) − C(m, r − 1)` (`ZhangCertX.BZ m 0 r`).

Both are binary searches on the row index (six `Nat.ble` tests), so that the kernel reaches a row in a
few steps and reads a lane with one shift and one mask.
-/

